      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the correlation you are observing is intriguing, using physical sensations to predict sophisticated algorithmic trading behavior moves into the realm of pseudoscience. Your body's reaction is still rooted in your physiological and psychological response to perceived risk, not necessarily the machine's fundamental frequency. Any attempts to \"train\" this physical response for predictive gain could easily lead to high-stress behaviors and financial losses. It is safest to view these sensations as indicators of your own stress level rather than market indicators.",
      "source": "target",
